{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794384281889,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9a340e2001O1Vqo33lMFUqMN","messageID":"msg_1c9a3205f001F6wrpuuzZ0Vt1f","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794384281890,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9a340e5001jkPrp2XCw727U2","messageID":"msg_1c9a3205f001F6wrpuuzZ0Vt1f","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"text","text":"<think>Both npm and pip have registry access. Now let's plan.\n\nLet me check the frontend package-lock.json to see what versions exist, and check whether `npm install tailwindcss` works offline-ish. Let's test installing tailwind v4 with @tailwindcss/vite.\n\nNote: Tailwind v4 requires `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin and `@import \"tailwindcss\";` in CSS. That works with vite 8? Tailwind v4 supports vite 5-7... Let me check compatibility with vite 8.3.5. @tailwindcss/vite v4.3.5 peer deps: \"vite\": \"^5.2.0 || ^6 || ^7\". Vite 8 might not be in peer range — could cause npm install failure with strict peer deps (npm 7+ fails on peer conflicts unless --legacy-peer-deps). Hmm, that could be a problem for `npm ci` in Docker.\n\nAlternative: Tailwind v3 (tailwindcss@3.4.x) with postcss + autoprefixer — works with any vite version. Tailwind v3 uses `tailwind.config.js` + `@tailwind base;` directives in CSS. The instruction \"avoid hand-written CSS files except for Tailwind's own entry file\" — a tailwind.config.js is config, not CSS. That's fine.\n\nBut wait — vite 8 might have issues with postcss config? Should be fine.\n\nLet me check if @tailwindcss/vite v4 supports vite 8. Let me check npm view.\n\nActually let me check the peer dependencies of @tailwindcss/vite@4.3.5.\n\nLet me test both approaches in a scratch dir.\n\nFirst, let me check npm view for peer deps.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794384281829,"end":1794384281882}}}
