{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794384380576,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9a4c271001jJzoSbpviS2m81","messageID":"msg_1c9a48ac3001EguHRGUAzIyXXH","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794384380576,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9a4c274001HokJ06U0zf0ag6","messageID":"msg_1c9a48ac3001EguHRGUAzIyXXH","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait, there's an issue with `init_db()` being called at import: `get_db()` uses `g`, which requires an app context. At module import time, there's no app context, so `g.db` would fail. I need to wrap in `with app.app_context():`.\n\nAlso `handle_unexpected` registered with `@app.errorhandler(Exception)` — this catches all exceptions including ApiError? ApiError has its own handler, and Flask picks the most specific handler. Should be fine. But careful: HTTPException subclasses (like 404) have their own handlers registered too.\n\nAlso, the generic Exception handler will catch werkzeug HTTPExceptions not specifically handled (e.g. 400 from bad JSON). Let me handle HTTPException properly: check `isinstance(error, HTTPException)` and return its response. Let me restructure: register a handler for HTTPException that returns JSON for /api paths.\n\nLet me fix these.\n\nAnother issue: `validate_store_payload` with `require_phone` param — I never use require_phone=True. Remove the param? Keep it simple: remove.\n\nAlso for PUT: \"an omitted phone is cleared\" — my code sets phone to None when absent. Good. But note the phone field: if body has \"phone\": \"\" → stripped to None → cleared. Fine.\n\nOne more: in `list_stores`, `q` searching also in phone. Fine.\n\nAlso `has_lat != has_lng` → 400. Hmm, is that risky? If a test sends only lat expecting normal list... unlikely. But a test might send `lat=0&lng=0`? has_lat is True since \"0\" != \"\". Good. But what about `lat=0`? `lat_raw is not None and lat_raw != \"\"` → \"0\" != \"\" → True. Good.\n\nHmm wait, what if a client sends lat but the API should just ignore it? I think 400 is fine and more correct.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: \"GET /api/stores lists stores sorted by name; with lat and lng it keeps the stores within radius kilometres\". A test might call `?lat=52.52&lng=13.405` without radius expecting nearest-first ordering with distance_km. My implementation handles that (no radius → no filtering, sorted by distance). Good.\n\nNow let me also double check the \"distance_km\" rounding: rounding to 3 decimals. Fine.\n\nAnother thought on `serialize_store` for a single store GET: distance_km is None. The spec says a store is returned with `distance_km` field. When fetching one store without location, null is right.\n\nLet me fix the init_db app context and HTTPException handling.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794384380532,"end":1794384380573}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794384380589,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_kOjdDPN0ESRo2yIS1ktN2bhl","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","newString":"from flask import Flask, g, jsonify, request, send_from_directory\nfrom werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException","oldString":"from flask import Flask, g, jsonify, request, send_from_directory"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -16,8 +16,9 @@\n from pathlib import Path\n from typing import Any\n \n from flask import Flask, g, jsonify, request, send_from_directory\n+from werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\n \n BASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n DATA_DIR = Path(os.environ.get(\"STORE_FINDER_DATA_DIR\") or (BASE_DIR / \"data\"))\n DB_PATH = DATA_DIR / \"store_finder.db\"\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/backend/app.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -16,8 +16,9 @@\n from pathlib import Path\n from typing import Any\n \n from flask import Flask, g, jsonify, request, send_from_directory\n+from werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\n \n BASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n DATA_DIR = Path(os.environ.get(\"STORE_FINDER_DATA_DIR\") or (BASE_DIR / \"data\"))\n DB_PATH = DATA_DIR / \"store_finder.db\"\n","additions":1,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/app.py","time":{"start":1794384380547,"end":1794384380586}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c9a4c279001QFiFq2NhDHN3oz","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","messageID":"msg_1c9a48ac3001EguHRGUAzIyXXH"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794384380601,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_FWd6w0CYYG0c5Wh7sZgBI1XB","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","newString":"@app.errorhandler(Exception)\ndef handle_unexpected(error: Exception):\n    if isinstance(error, ApiError):\n        return handle_api_error(error)\n    if isinstance(error, HTTPException):\n        payload = {\n            \"error\": error.description or error.name,\n            \"code\": error.name.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\"),\n        }\n        return jsonify(payload), error.code\n    app.logger.exception(\"unhandled error: %s\", error)\n    return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error.\", \"code\": \"server_error\"}), 500","oldString":"@app.errorhandler(Exception)\ndef handle_unexpected(error: Exception):\n    if isinstance(error, ApiError):\n        return handle_api_error(error)\n    app.logger.exception(\"unhandled error: %s\", error)\n    if request.path.startswith(\"/api/\"):\n        return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error.\", \"code\": \"server_error\"}), 500\n    return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error.\", \"code\": \"server_error\"}), 500"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -326,11 +326,15 @@\n @app.errorhandler(Exception)\n def handle_unexpected(error: Exception):\n     if isinstance(error, ApiError):\n         return handle_api_error(error)\n+    if isinstance(error, HTTPException):\n+        payload = {\n+            \"error\": error.description or error.name,\n+            \"code\": error.name.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\"),\n+        }\n+        return jsonify(payload), error.code\n     app.logger.exception(\"unhandled error: %s\", error)\n-    if request.path.