{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794384487426,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9a663f30010awHuEDw9bF6V7","messageID":"msg_1c9a6382a0015PGH5ie7l3Cw6B","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794384487426,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9a663f5001TkS4T4StNukuAW","messageID":"msg_1c9a6382a0015PGH5ie7l3Cw6B","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"text","text":"<think>The failures are due to shared state across tests: the DB persists between tests (same temp dir), so \"kim\" is already registered from a previous test, and the admin token from setUp... wait, 401 for create_store means the admin token was invalid. Why? Because `issue_token` inserts into the tokens table... the token should be valid. Hmm, unless the admin login failed in setUp: `self.admin_token = self.login(\"admin\", \"s3cret-admin\")` — that returns a response, not a token! Bug in my test: `login` returns the response object, not the token. So `self.admin_token` is a Response object → header \"Bearer <Response>\" → invalid → 401.\n\nLet me fix the test helper: make `login` return the token string, and add a separate `login_response` for status checks.\n\nAlso DB state leakage between tests: each test method uses the same DB. I should reset the DB per test (delete all rows) or create a fresh temp dir per test class. Simplest: in setUp, wipe the tables (delete from tokens, users, stores) and re-seed stores. But seeding is done at import. Let me add a helper in the test to reset: delete all users/tokens/stores, then re-insert sample stores via backend.seed_sample_stores().\n\nLet me restructure: add a `reset_database()` in setUp:\n\n```python\ndef setUp(self):\n    db = backend.get_db()  # needs app context\n    ...\n```\nget_db uses `g` → requires app context. I can use `with backend.app.app_context():`.\n\nLet me write:\n```python\ndef setUp(self):\n    self.client = backend.app.test_client()\n    with backend.app.app_context():\n        db = backend.get_db()\n        db.execute(\"DELETE FROM tokens\")\n        db.execute(\"DELETE FROM users\")\n        db.execute(\"DELETE FROM stores\")\n        db.commit()\n        backend.ensure_admin_user()\n        backend.seed_sample_stores()\n    ...\n```\n\nCareful: the `users` table has the admin user; deleting and recreating is fine.\n\nLet me update the test file.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794384487413,"end":1794384487423}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794384487450,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_AOMyyZFcYfxIdGHRaWNPyoKv","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/tests/test_api.py","newString":"class ApiTestCase(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.client = backend.app.test_client()\n        self.admin_password = os.environ.pop(\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\", None)\n        os.environ[\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\"] = \"s3cret-admin\"\n        with backend.app.app_context():\n            db = backend.get_db()\n            db.execute(\"DELETE FROM tokens\")\n            db.execute(\"DELETE FROM users\")\n            db.execute(\"DELETE FROM stores\")\n            db.commit()\n            backend.ensure_admin_user()\n            backend.seed_sample_stores()\n        self.admin_token = self.login_token(\"admin\", \"s3cret-admin\")\n\n    def tearDown(self):\n        if self.admin_password is None:\n            os.environ.pop(\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\", None)\n        else:\n            os.environ[\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\"] = self.admin_password\n\n    def login_token(self, username, password):\n        response = self.client.post(\n            \"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": password}\n        )\n        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200, response.get_data(as_text=True))\n        return response.get_json()[\"token\"]\n\n    def auth(self, token):\n        return {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}","oldString":"class ApiTestCase(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.client = backend.app.test_client()\n        self.admin_password = os.environ.pop(\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\", None)\n        os.environ[\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\"] = \"s3cret-admin\"\n        self.admin_token = self.login(\"admin\", \"s3cret-admin\")\n\n    def tearDown(self):\n        if self.admin_password is None:\n            os.environ.pop(\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\", None)\n        else:\n            os.environ[\"ADM