{"type":"text","timestamp":1794384716450,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9a9e28b0017C3aeX5CVEGh0x","messageID":"msg_1c9a9c5bd001h5fwcVLoNKLj2H","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"text","text":"<think>The build works. Now let me check TypeScript types compile. There's no `tsc` in the build script (vite build doesn't type-check by default with esbuild). Let me add a typecheck step: is `typescript` installed? Let me check node_modules for typescript. The package.json doesn't list typescript. The scaffold has no tsconfig.json either? Let me check.\n\nThe original scaffold: frontend/ has index.html, package.json, package-lock.json, src/, vite.config.ts. No tsconfig.json! Vite handles TS via esbuild without type-checking. But `vite.config.ts` is TS. Hmm, there's no tsconfig.json in the repo — that's how the scaffold was. Let me check for tsconfig files.\n\nAdding TypeScript + a typecheck script would be good practice (the task says React TypeScript). Let me add tsconfig.json and typescript as a devDependency, plus a \"typecheck\" script. This requires updating package-lock.json. Risk: `npm ci` in Docker must work — it will since the lock file is updated.\n\nLet me check if typescript is already in the lock file (maybe as a transitive dep).</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794384716427,"end":1794384716446}}}
