{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794384930508,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9ad26bd001T1F4W5v5pOky0A","messageID":"msg_1c9acc41e0017CZAd1lorhxjhl","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794384930508,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9ad26c00018RmtHNLjKVnjRH","messageID":"msg_1c9acc41e0017CZAd1lorhxjhl","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"text","text":"<think>The frontend renders correctly. Now let me extend the smoke test to also exercise interactions:\n1. Search box typing → triggers a fetch with q.\n2. Admin sign-in flow: click \"Admin sign-in\", fill the form, submit → session stored, admin panel appears.\n3. \"Use my location\" → geolocation permission denied → note shown, plain list stays.\n4. Delete confirmation flow.\n\nThat's valuable. Let me enhance the smoke test with interactions using React's synthetic events in jsdom. Dispatching events: for React 19, use `element.value = \"x\"` then dispatch an \"input\" event with bubbles: true. React listens to the \"input\" event for controlled inputs. For select changes, dispatch a \"change\" event.\n\nFor clicks: `element.dispatchEvent(new window.MouseEvent(\"click\", {bubbles: true}))`.\n\nLet me write these interactions carefully:\n\nTest A: search\n- find input[type=\"search\"], set value \"berlin\", dispatch input event → wait 300ms (debounce) → check that a request \"GET /api/stores?q=berlin\" was made.\n\nTest B: geolocation denied\n- navigator.geolocation is undefined in jsdom → my code checks `\"geolocation\" in navigator` → jsdom's navigator doesn't have geolocation → shows \"This browser cannot share a location — showing all stores.\" Hmm, I want to test the PERMISSION_DENIED path. I can define `window.navigator.geolocation = { getCurrentPosition: (ok, err) => err({code: 1, PERMISSION_DENIED: 1}) }`. Then click \"Use my location\" → expect the note \"Location permission denied — showing all stores.\" and the list still shows stores.\n\nNote: my code references the global `navigator` — in the browser it's `window.navigator`; in the bundle, `navigator` resolves to globalThis.navigator which I defined as window.navigator. If I add geolocation to window.navigator, it should be visible. jsdom's navigator is a getter-only property but I can define `geolocation` on it via Object.defineProperty(navigator, 'geolocation', {...}).\n\nTest C: admin sign-in\n- Click \"Admin sign-in\" button → the form appears.\n- Fill username/password inputs (type=text/password) → set values and dispatch input events.\n- Submit the form (dispatch submit event on the form, or click the submit button).\n- Then the admin panel \"Manage directory\" should appear, and the \"Add store\" button.\n\nLet me also test the delete confirmation: click \"Delete\" on a store → \"Delete this store?\" appears.\n\nFor the store list items, the buttons appear only when isAdmin. The session restore effect calls /api/auth/me which my stub returns as admin → so the admin panel appears on load (after the effect resolves). Let me confirm the effect ran: the stub returns is_admin: true. So after ~200ms, \"Manage directory\" should be in the DOM. Wait — but the localStorage token is empty on first load, so the restore effect returns early and no session exists. So the admin UI won't appear unless I sign in. Good — Test C covers it.\n\nLet me restructure the smoke test to do these steps in sequence with helper functions.\n\nReact event simulation details: For React 19 with jsdom, setting `input.value` directly doesn't trigger React's onChange because React tracks the value via a value setter on the element. The standard workaround is to use the native value setter:\n\n```js\nfunction setNativeValue(element, value) {\n  const setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, \"value\").set;\n  setter.call(element, value);\n  element.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\n}\n```\nThis is the well-known approach. Let me use that.\n\nFor a select: `setNativeValue(select, \"25\"); select.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"change\", {bubbles: true}))`.\n\nLet me write the enhanced test.\n\nAlso note React 19 uses `onChange` for input → listens to \"input\" event. Good.\n\nLet me rewrite the smoke test file with these interactions.</think>\n\nThe frontend renders. Let me extend the smoke test to cover the interactive flows.","time":{"start":1794384930496,"end":1794384930506}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794384930538,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_fLbSAeQRSo9KALees1q2bfnq","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"/**\n * Smoke test for the built frontend bundle.\n *\n * Loads the production bundle in jsdom against a stubbed API and checks that\n * the store list, the search box, the location button and the admin flows\n * behave.\n *\n * Run with: node frontend/tests/smoke.mjs\n */\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { dirname, join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from \"node:url\";\nimport { JSDOM } from \"jsdom\";\n\nconst here = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst dist = join(here, \"..\", \"dist\");\n\nconst stores = [\n  {\n    id: 1,\n    name: \"Alte Post Markt\",\n    address: \"Hauptstrasse 12, 10115 Berlin\",\n    phone: \"+49 30 5550101\",\n    latitude: 52.5291,\n    longitude: 13.405,\n    distance_km: null,\n  },\n  {\n    id: 2,\n    name: \"HafenCity Provisions\",\n    address: \"Am Sandtorkai 42, 20457 Hamburg\",\n    phone: null,\n    latitude: 53.5411,\n    longitude: 9.9931,\n    distance_km: null,\n  },\n];\n\nconst requests = [];\nlet adminToken = null;\n\nfunction jsonResponse(body, status = 200) {\n  return {\n    ok: status >= 200 && status < 300,\n    status,\n    text: async () => JSON.stringify(body),\n  };\n}\n\nconst dom = new JSDOM('<!doctype html><html><body><div id=\"root\"></div></body></html>', {\n  url: \"http://localhost/\",\n  pretendToBeVisual: true,\n});\n\nconst { window } = dom;\nglobalThis.window = window;\nglobalThis.document = window.document;\nObject.defineProperty(globalThis, \"navigator\", { value: window.navigator, configurable: true });\nglobalThis.HTMLElement = window.HTMLElement;\nglobalThis.Element = window.Element;\nglobalThis.Node = window.Node;\nglobalThis.Event = window.Event;\nglobalThis.MouseEvent = window.MouseEvent;\nglobalThis.KeyboardEvent = window.KeyboardEvent;\nglobalThis.getComputedStyle = window.getComputedStyle;\nglobalThis.MutationObserver = window.MutationObserver;\nglobalThis.CustomEvent = window.CustomEvent;\nglobalThis.location = window.location;\nglobalThis.history = window.history;\nglobalThis.requestAnimationFrame = (cb) => setTimeout(() => cb(Date.now()), 0);\nglobalThis.cancelAnimationFrame = (id) => clearTimeout(id);\n\nconst storage = new Map();\nObject.defineProperty(window, \"localStorage\", {\n  value: {\n    getItem: (key) => (storage.has(key) ? storage.get(key) : null),\n    setItem: (key, value) => storage.set(key, String(value)),\n    removeItem: (key) => storage.delete(key),\n    clear: () => storage.clear(),\n  },\n});\n\nglobalThis.fetch = async (url, init = {}) => {\n  requests.push(`${init.method ?? \"GET\"} ${url}`);\n  const path = String(url);\n  if (path.startsWith(\"/api/stores\")) {\n    return jsonResponse({ items: stores });\n  }\n  if (path.startsWith(\"/api/auth/me\")) {\n    return jsonResponse({ user: { username: \"admin\", is_admin: true } });\n  }\n  if (path.startsWith(\"/api/auth/login\")) {\n    adminToken = \"test-token\";\n    return jsonResponse({ token: adminToken, username: \"admin\", is_admin: true });\n  }\n  if (path.startsWith(\"/api/admin/stores\") && (init.method ?? \"GET\") === \"DELETE\") {\n    return { ok: true, status: 204, text: async () => \"\" };\n  }\n  return jsonResponse({ error: \"not found\" }, 404);\n};\n\nconst assets = join(dist, \"assets\");\nconst bundle = readdirSync(assets).find((file) => file.endsWith(\".js\"));\nif (!bundle) {\n  throw new Error(\"No built bundle found. Run `npm run build` first.\");\n}\n\nawait import(pathToFileURL(join(assets, bundle)).href);\n\nconst failures = [];\n\nfunction check(label, condition, extra = \"\") {\n  if (condition) {\n    console.log(`ok   ${label}`);\n  } else {\n    failures.push(`${label} ${extra}`);\n    console.log(`FAIL ${label} ${extra}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction wait(ms = 120) {\n  return new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));\n}\n\nfunction html() {\n  return window.document.body.innerHTML;\n}\n\nfunction byText(selector, text) {\n  return Array.from(window.document.querySelectorAll(selector)).find((element) =>\n    (element.textContent ?? \"\").trim().includes(text),\n  );\n}\n\nfunction setNativeValue(element, value) {\n  const prototype =\n    element.tagName === \"SELECT\"\n      ? window.HTMLSelectElement.prototype\n      : window.HTMLInputElement.prototype;\n  const setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(prototype, \"value\").set;\n  setter.call(element, value);\n  element.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\n  element.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"change\", { bubbles: true }));\n}\n\nfunction click(element) {\n  element.dispatchEvent(new window.MouseEvent(\"click\", { bubbles: true }));\n}\n\nawait wait(300);\n\ncheck(\"renders the heading\", html().includes(\"Store finder\"));\ncheck(\"lists the seeded stores\", html().includes(\"Alte Post Markt\"));\ncheck(\"shows an address\", html().includes(\"Hauptstrasse 12, 10115 Berlin\"));\ncheck(\"shows a phone number\", html().includes(\"+49 30 5550101\"));\ncheck(\"renders the search box\", html().includes(\"Search stores\"));\ncheck(\"renders the location button\", html().includes(\"Use my location\"));\ncheck(\"renders the radius selector\", html().includes(\"Radius\"));\ncheck(\"renders the map plot\", html().includes(\"Latitude / longitude plot\"));\ncheck(\n  \"requests the store list\",\n  requests.some((entry) => entry.startsWith(\"GET /api/stores\")),\n  JSON.stringify(requests),\n);\ncheck(\n  \"plots the stores in the svg\",\n  html().includes(\"<svg\") && html().includes(\"Alte Post Markt</text>\"),\n);\n\nconst searchInput = window.document.querySelector('input[type=\"search\"]');\nsetNativeValue(searchInput, \"berlin\");\nawait wait(500);\ncheck(\n  \"searches through the api\",\n  requests.some((entry) => entry.includes(\"/api/stores?q=berlin\")),\n  JSON.stringify(requests),\n);\n\nObject.defineProperty(window.navigator, \"geolocation\", {\n  configurable: true,\n  value: {\n    getCurrentPosition: (_ok, fail) =>\n      fail({ code: 1, PERMISSION_DENIED: 1, message: \"denied\" }),\n  },\n});\nclick(byText(\"button\", \"Use my location\"));\nawait wait(200);\ncheck(\n  \"shows a note when location permission is denied\",\n  html().includes(\"Location permission denied\"),\n);\ncheck(\"keeps the plain list after a denied location\", html().includes(\"Alte Post Markt\"));\ncheck(\n  \"does not request coordinates after a denied location\",\n  !requests.some((entry) => entry.includes(\"lat=\")),\n  JSON.stringify(requests),\n);\n\nclick(byText(\"button\", \"Admin sign-in\"));\nawait wait(120);\ncheck(\"opens the sign-in form\", html().includes(\"Admin sign-in</h2>\"));\nconst passwordInput = window.document.querySelector('input[type=\"password\"]');\nsetNativeValue(passwordInput, \"adminpass\");\nconst usernameInput = window.document.querySelector('input[name=\"username\"]');\nsetNativeValue(usernameInput, \"admin\");\nawait wait(120);\nconst form = window.document.querySelector(\"form\");\nform.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"submit\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\nawait wait(300);\ncheck(\"signs the admin in\", adminToken !== null);\ncheck(\"shows the directory management panel\", html().includes(\"Manage directory\"));\ncheck(\"stores the token\", storage.get(\"store-finder.token\") === \"test-token\");\ncheck(\n  \"shows edit and delete actions\",\n  html().includes(\"Edit\") && html().includes(\"Delete\"),\n);\n\nclick(byText(\"button\", \"Delete\"));\nawait wait(120);\ncheck(\"asks for delete confirmation\", html().includes(\"Delete this store?\"));\n\nclick(byText(\"button\", \"Add store\"));\nawait wait(120);\ncheck(\"opens the add form\", html().includes(\"Add a store\"));\n\nconst indexHtml = readFileSync(join(dist, \"index.html\"), \"utf8\");\ncheck(\"ships a stylesheet\", /assets\\/.*\\.css/.test(indexHtml));\n\nif (failures.length > 0) {\n  console.error(`\\n${failures.length} check(s) failed`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\nconsole.log(\"\\nfrontend smoke test passed\");\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/tests/smoke.mjs","time":{"start":1794384930502,"end":1794384930514}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c9ad26c2001P20iOfiNZXb9K3","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","messageID":"msg_1c9acc41e0017CZAd1lorhxjhl"}}
