{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794384952368,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9ad7c1c001rP4WfNgYdLd0dE","messageID":"msg_1c9ad57b5001as5wEYE4F6BXm1","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794384952368,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"id":"prt_1c9ad7c1f001Jsu3M8Wb7Uajkv","messageID":"msg_1c9ad57b5001as5wEYE4F6BXm1","sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","type":"text","text":"<think>Excellent — all frontend interactions work. Now let me add the smoke test script to package.json as \"test\": \"node tests/smoke.mjs\" so it can be run easily. And add a build+test ordering note.\n\nAlso, I should double check the \"Use my location\" success path (with coordinates) — the plot should show the visitor and the list should show distances. Let me add that to the smoke test: after the denied test, redefine geolocation to succeed with coordinates and check that the request includes lat/lng/radius and that the store list shows \"km away\" and the plot shows \"You are here\".\n\nThe stub returns stores with distance_km: null though. Let me make the stub compute distance_km when lat/lng are present: if the URL contains \"lat=\", return stores with distance_km set. That better mimics the API.\n\nLet me update the stub:\n```js\nif (path.startsWith(\"/api/stores\")) {\n  const url = new URL(path, \"http://localhost\");\n  const lat = url.searchParams.get(\"lat\");\n  const lng = url.searchParams.get(\"lng\");\n  const radius = url.searchParams.get(\"radius\");\n  let items = stores;\n  if (lat && lng) {\n    items = stores.map(s => ({...s, distance_km: Math.round(Math.hypot(s.latitude-lat, s.longitude-lng)*100)/100}));\n    if (radius) items = items.filter(s => s.distance_km <= Number(radius));\n  }\n  return jsonResponse({items});\n}\n```\n\nThen the location success test: geolocation returns coords (52.52, 13.405), radius default 10 → request \"/api/stores?lat=52.52&lng=13.405&radius=10\" → items with distance_km → the UI shows \"km away\" and the plot shows \"You are here\".\n\nLet me add that.\n\nAlso I want to test the radius selector change → request with the new radius.\n\nLet me update the test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794384952351,"end":1794384952365}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794384952401,"sessionID":"ses_e365d97c7ffelqEqEaqM6zrsDt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_Vvpa3PN3drlEtNu0VPWqvrDE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs","newString":"globalThis.fetch = async (url, init = {}) => {\n  requests.push(`${init.method ?? \"GET\"} ${url}`);\n  const path = String(url);\n  if (path.startsWith(\"/api/stores\")) {\n    const parsed = new URL(path, \"http://localhost\");\n    const lat = parsed.searchParams.get(\"lat\");\n    const lng = parsed.searchParams.get(\"lng\");\n    const radius = parsed.searchParams.get(\"radius\");\n    let items = stores;\n    if (lat && lng) {\n      items = stores.map((store) => ({\n        ...store,\n        distance_km:\n          Math.round(Math.hypot(store.latitude - Number(lat), store.longitude - Number(lng)) * 100) /\n          100,\n      }));\n      if (radius) {\n        items = items.filter((store) => store.distance_km <= Number(radius));\n      }\n    }\n    return jsonResponse({ items });\n  }","oldString":"globalThis.fetch = async (url, init = {}) => {\n  requests.push(`${init.method ?? \"GET\"} ${url}`);\n  const path = String(url);\n  if (path.startsWith(\"/api/stores\")) {\n    return jsonResponse({ items: stores });\n  }"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs\n+++ /workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs\n@@ -83,9 +83,25 @@\n globalThis.fetch = async (url, init = {}) => {\n   requests.push(`${init.method ?? \"GET\"} ${url}`);\n   const path = String(url);\n   if (path.startsWith(\"/api/stores\")) {\n-    return jsonResponse({ items: stores });\n+    const parsed = new URL(path, \"http://localhost\");\n+    const lat = parsed.searchParams.get(\"lat\");\n+    const lng = parsed.searchParams.get(\"lng\");\n+    const radius = parsed.searchParams.get(\"radius\");\n+    let items = stores;\n+    if (lat && lng) {\n+      items = stores.map((store) => ({\n+        ...store,\n+        distance_km:\n+          Math.round(Math.hypot(store.latitude - Number(lat), store.longitude - Number(lng)) * 100) /\n+          100,\n+      }));\n+      if (radius) {\n+        items = items.filter((store) => store.distance_km <= Number(radius));\n+      }\n+    }\n+    return jsonResponse({ items });\n   }\n   if (path.startsWith(\"/api/auth/me\")) {\n     return jsonResponse({ user: { username: \"admin\", is_admin: true } });\n   }\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs\n+++ /workspace/frontend/tests/smoke.mjs\n@@ -83,9 +83,25 @@\n globalThis.fetch = async (url, init = {}) => {\n   requests.push(`${init.method ?? \"GET\"} ${url}`);\n   const path = String(url);\n   if (path.startsWith(\"/api/stores\")) {\n-    return jsonResponse({ items: stores });\n+    const parsed = new URL(path, \"http://localhost\");\n+    const lat = parsed.searchParams.get(\"lat\");\n+    const lng = parsed.searchParams.get(\"lng\");\n+    const radius = parsed.searchParams.get(\"radius\");\n+    let items = stores;\n+    if (lat && lng) {\n+      items = stores.map((store) => ({\n+        ...store,\n+        distance_km:\n+          Math.round(Math.hypot(store.latitude - Number(lat), store.longitude - Number(lng)) * 100) /\n+          100,\n+      }));\n+      if (radius) {\n+        items = items.filter((store) => store.distance_km <= Number(radius));\n+      }\n+    }\n+    return jsonResponse({ items });\n   }\n   if (path.startsWith(\"/api/auth/me\")) {\n     return jsonResponse({ user: { username: \"admin\", is_admin: true } });\n   }\n","additions":17,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/tests/smoke.mjs","time":{"start":1